<title>POLAND: Poland raises T-bill offer to PLN 5.7 bln in April.</title>
<headline>Poland raises T-bill offer to PLN 5.7 bln in April.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Finance Ministry increased its T-bill offer to 5.7 billion zlotys in April from 4.9 billion in March, it said.</p>
<p>According to its preliminary plan, which can be changed, the ministry will not offer 39-week bills next month.  </p>
<p>TENTATIVE APRIL T-BILL OFFER SCHEDULE (in million zlotys)</p>
<p>	    April 1  April 7  April 14  April 21  April 28</p>
<p>   8-week     0	 0	   0	 200	  200</p>
<p>  13-week   200     300	 300	 300	  300</p>
<p>  26-week   200     200	 200	 200	  200</p>
<p>  39-week     0	 0	   0	   0	    0</p>
<p>  52-week   600     600	 600	 600	  500</p>
<p>   TOTAL   1000    1100	1100	1300	 1200</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
